# .gitignore — calcium-cholesterol analysis
#
# Paths here are anchored to this directory. Generic, path-free rules (OS junk,
# R session files, *_cache/, logs/) live in the repo-root .gitignore and apply
# recursively, so they are not repeated here.
#
# Rule of thumb: anything reproducible from a script or a render stays out of git.
# Without the raw_data rules below, `git add -A` stages ~5 GB.

# ---- Downloaded data and reference panels (robust MR arm, ~4.9 GB) ------------
# All regenerable via scripts/fetch_robust_mr_data.sh.
raw_data/robust_mr/
raw_data/reference/

# ---- PheWeb / consortium summary statistics (~649 MB) --------------------------
# The phenocode-*.tsv.gz files are MGI-BioVU LabWAS results, restricted to
# University of Michigan researchers and NOT redistributable (see README.md
# "Reproducibility Notes"). The GEFOS/fracture files are public but large and
# re-downloadable. Ignore the data, keep the provenance README tracked.
PheWeb Summary Statistics/*
!PheWeb Summary Statistics/README.md

# Harmonised intermediates and fitted model objects (regenerable from prep)
raw_data/robust_mr/cache/

# ---- Quarto asset directories --------------------------------------------------
# The robust_mr_*.qmd files set embed-resources: true, so their .html is
# self-contained and these are disposable. Do NOT add a blanket *_files/ rule —
# the older analyses here are not self-contained and their committed .html would
# render unstyled without them.
robust_mr_*_files/

# ---- GWAS Catalog FTP summary statistics (~1 GB per accession) ----------------
# Public and re-downloadable; drug_target_mr_bmd.qmd fetches GCST90726625
# (Chai 2026 heel eBMD) here automatically on first render.
raw_data/gwas_catalog/
